From aca8c029ac49a83eb7cfacb7bb3b1956cab2f1fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:11:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] avcodec: add native AC-4 encoder

lavc wrapper (ENCODE_CB) registering the ff_ac4_encoder codec,
wiring the C1/C2 objects live: allcodecs extern, wrapper OBJS,
configure per-flag probe feeding CFLAGS-ac4enc_float (per-object
only, never global), Changelog entry.
First patch defining codec behavior.

Re-cut (r3): harden the two wrapper s64 sites found by fuzzing
(FUZZ-CENC crash-1 pts_base add -> av_sat_add64, crash-3
bit_rate + 500 -> top-500 early EINVAL); behavior otherwise
identical to r2.

Re-cut (r6): M10 _tab in the float-discipline list; M11 carry
AV_CODEC_CAP_EXPERIMENTAL (fate CMDs take -strict -2 in 05/10 and
08/10); M12 drop ENCODER_REORDERED_OPAQUE (unplumbed); M13
configure-probe sincos; M15 wrapper reads ctx-carried
ac4enc_err_detail; M16 drop the lavc minor bump (no public API
change). Encoder bytes unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
---
 Changelog              |   1 +
 configure              |  19 ++
 libavcodec/Makefile    |  17 ++
 libavcodec/ac4enc.c    | 643 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libavcodec/ac4enc.h    |  73 +++++
 libavcodec/allcodecs.c |   1 +
 6 files changed, 754 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libavcodec/ac4enc.c
 create mode 100644 libavcodec/ac4enc.h

diff --git a/Changelog b/Changelog
index 8bff2da..df0e93f 100644
--- a/Changelog
+++ b/Changelog
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ Entries are sorted chronologically from oldest to youngest within each release,
 releases are sorted from youngest to oldest.
 
 version <next>:
+- native AC-4 audio encoder
 - ASTC image encoding and decoding via libastcenc, with .astc and KTX 1.0 muxers and demuxers
 - extensively improved AAC encoder
 - APV Vulkan encoder
diff --git a/configure b/configure
index c97ddb1..9c3f59e 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -2553,6 +2553,7 @@ SYSTEM_FUNCS="
     setrlimit
     sigaction
     siglongjmp
+    sincos
     Sleep
     strerror_r
     sysconf
@@ -7957,6 +7958,23 @@ check_optflags $optflags
 check_optflags -fno-math-errno
 check_optflags -fno-signed-zeros
 
+# AC-4 encoder float discipline: probe per-flag, apply per-object
+# only (libavcodec/Makefile consumes CFLAGS-ac4enc_float). Probes a
+# toolchain rejects with an error fail closed; ones it merely warns
+# about (e.g. cl D9002, exit 0) still land in the var but are
+# ignored, hence harmless. Default cl /fp:precise already satisfies
+# the discipline (no contraction, no libm rewrites, signed zeros
+# kept), and the global -fno-signed-zeros never reaches MSVC either.
+ac4enc_float_cflags=""
+for ac4flag in -ffp-contract=off -fno-builtin-sin -fno-builtin-cos \
+               -fno-builtin-pow -fsigned-zeros; do
+    test_cflags "$ac4flag" && \
+        ac4enc_float_cflags="$ac4enc_float_cflags $ac4flag"
+done
+# M13: probe sincos(3) for libavcodec/ac4_loudness.c. Toolchains
+# without it (e.g. MSVC) take the separate sin()+cos() fallback.
+check_func_headers math.h sincos -lm
+
