From 94306f8aee9cf824ffc1d45bcbb644082352c788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:11:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] doc: AC-4 encoder docs

@anchor{ac4} section in encoders.texi documenting the 6 private
options (iframe_interval, priming, short_blocks, joint_shorts,
measure_loudness, loudness_target) with the 48k-only, CBR-only,
whole-stream-buffered behavior notes plus the experimental/limits
notes; the audio-table AC-4 row becomes the single @tab IX @tab IX
row (this series stacks on the decoder docs, which carry the decode
column).

Re-cut (r6): M18 single-row merge onto the decoder row (drops the
second-row brag); M11 experimental + limits paragraph.

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
---
 doc/encoders.texi         | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 doc/general_contents.texi |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/encoders.texi b/doc/encoders.texi
index 2c173ac..28f66c9 100644
--- a/doc/encoders.texi
+++ b/doc/encoders.texi
@@ -541,6 +541,54 @@ Selected by Encoder (default)
 
 @end table
 
+@anchor{ac4}
+@section ac4
+
+Dolby AC-4 audio encoder, natively implemented into FFmpeg.
+
+The encoder buffers the whole stream, runs a loudness-measure pass at
+flush (matching file-mode behavior), and emits one raw AC-4 frame per
+packet. Only 48 kHz stereo and 5.1 input are supported (resample with
+@code{-af aresample}); the output bitrate snaps to the supported
+constant-bitrate steps. Constant bit rate only: @code{-q:a} (VBR) is
+rejected.
+
+The encoder is experimental: pass @code{-strict -2} (or @code{-strict
+experimental}) to select it. Limits of this version: the whole input
+is buffered in memory before any output is emitted (tens of MB for a
+typical song); inputs past ~1.07B samples per channel are refused;
+the default loudness correction may refuse full-scale material at
+the loudness floor (use @code{loudness_target=0} to skip the
+correction gain). A streaming (low-memory) mode is planned but not
+implemented here.
+
+@subsection Options
+
+@table @option
+@item iframe_interval @var{string}
+I-frame interval: @samp{1sec} (default) or a frame step >= 2.
+
+@item priming @var{boolean}
+Write the priming frame (default 1). Stereo only in effect: the 5.1
+path is priming-only and rejects @code{priming=0}.
+
+@item short_blocks @var{boolean}
+Allow short-block transients (default 1).
+
+@item joint_shorts @var{boolean}
+Joint-stereo short blocks (default 0). Stereo only: rejected for 5.1.
+
+@item measure_loudness @var{boolean}
+Run the pass-1 loudness measure at flush (default 1). When disabled,
+the encoder takes the neutral path (no loudness correction), whose
+output differs from file mode by design.
+
+@item loudness_target @var{double}
+Target loudness in LUFS: 0 or -31..-10 (default -24). 0 keeps the
+measure path but skips the correction gain; use it when the input is
+refused at the loudness floor.
+@end table
+
 @anchor{flac}
 @section flac
 
